  "prompt_text": "The figure compares four classes of mechanical or elastic metamaterial behavior, organized by the signs of two parameters labeled \\(K\\) and \\(\\rho\\). Taken together, it shows how different combinations of positive or negative effective stiffness and mass density can be realized by distinct structures.\n\nOne panel uses a water-like scene with concentric ripples and a vertical chain of droplets to suggest an ordinary medium with both quantities positive, where waves propagate in the familiar way. The other panels replace this with schematic unit-cell designs. For negative stiffness with positive density, the image shows repeating frame-like geometries above a solid base, implying a structured lattice that alters the elastic response through shape. For positive stiffness with negative density, a resonant mass–spring picture appears: a central blue mass is suspended by springs inside a ring, above a layered support, emphasizing internal resonance as the source of unusual effective inertia. When both \\(K\\) and \\(\\rho\\) are negative, the figure combines structured beams with resonant connections and ends with a compact labyrinth-like geometry, suggesting a composite architecture engineered to produce both effects simultaneously.\n\nOverall, the message is that tailored microstructures and resonators can create unconventional effective wave properties.",
